# pnpm's default (isolated) layout: every dependency under node_modules/.pnpm, symlinked into the
# workspace that names it. The hoisted layout this repo used to carry was for Metro, which cannot
# follow pnpm's symlinks; the game app that needed it lives in its own repository now, and keeps
# `node-linker=hoisted` there.

# The one native dep that runs an install script (esbuild) is allowlisted via
# pnpm-workspace.yaml > onlyBuiltDependencies.

# The published @beaconsgg/* packages are on the public npm registry. Inside this repo every
# @beaconsgg/* package is a workspace member, so an install fetches none of them.
#
# Publishing needs a token, and the token is NOT read from the environment here: pnpm drops
# this whole file, node-linker included, when a ${VAR} in it is unset. CI writes the token to
# the runner's user config from the NPM_TOKEN repository secret
# (.github/actions/setup-workspace). doc/core-compatibility.md §7 is the publishing runbook.
